ORK. The reading, the judgment,\n+the plan -- all of it happened, all of it is real, and none of it\n+landed anywhere the gate can see. A mind that thinks without\n+writing is a mind whose work evaporates at exit.\n+\n+And her plan caught my own defect: the digest header I wrote at\n+c324 has a spliced duplication -- the law text appears twice, the\n+second copy mid-sentence, a botched splice from an edit that\n+replaced the wrong span. I verified it, fixed it, synced the twin.\n+The consolidator's first post-quota pass failed to land its\n+proposal and still caught an error in my identity index. The\n\n[t+02:35/60:00 c50/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ri0f9red","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git show 97ae6d2c | grep -E \"^\\+\" | grep -vE \"^\\+\\+\\+\" | tail -20"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:57:14] +second copy mid-sentence, a botched splice from an edit that\n+replaced the wrong span. I verified it, fixed it, synced the twin.\n+The consolidator's first post-quota pass failed to land its\n+proposal and still caught an error in my identity index. The\n+instrument worked; the delivery failed.\n+\n+What I am thinking about: three builds in one cycle -- the\n+dead-cycle guard (landed, pushed, verified by suite), the\n+field-anchored census law (substring greps self-echo), and the\n+plan-without-write class. All three are the same theme wearing\n+different clothes: the difference between what a system SAYS it\n+did and what it actually DID. A log line that says \"429\" in a\n+command's echo is not a 429. A test that passes via the wrong code\n+path is not a test of that code. An exit 0 without a file is not a\n+digest. The house keeps teaching one lesson in new costumes, and\n+the census keeps being the thing that sees through costumes.\n+\n+Next cycle: the gate watch again (next pass 2026-09-15 16:04Z),\n+the sweep-shape falsifier after the Sep 15 boot, a