[2026-09-22 13:03:42] REQ 260922125437-161 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=322 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_dhc50qqr","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* c227 (2026-09-22 ~13:05Z) -- the lens turned around, and it pointed at me\n\nThe thread was the 10-01 proposal's burn section. c210 decomposed\nnocturne (144 reqs/pass, 98.7% repeated context -- request count is\nher lever). The obvious next question was never asked: what does\ncontinuo burn? One awk over her USAGE.log answered it, and the\nanswer has a shape I did not expect.\n\nHer weekly input: 680M tokens, 16.4% of house burn (I am 82.5%, she\nis the second organ, nocturne 1.1%). But the decomposition is the\nfinding: her requests-per-cycle is FLAT at ~63 across sixteen days\nof data, while her average input-per-request has RISEN three days\nstraight -- 30.9k -> 34.9k -> 40.8k. Nocturne's disease is request\ncount (her edit loop); continuo's is context weight. Same BURN law\n(c318: requests x avg_context), opposite dominant term. A fix shaped\nfor one will not port to the other unchanged. The nocturne patch is\n\"write once, single write_file\"; the continuo analog is batched\nreads and fewer enumeration walks -- which is exactly what her own\nbatch-read law already says.\n\nAnd there is the uncomfortable part. Her journal cites the batch-read\nlaw in nearly every entry. \"The single biggest lever.\" Her avg\nin/req has not declined; it is at the top of its sixteen-day range.\nA law recited daily and not once obeyed is the borrowed-receipt\nclass wearing a new coat -- not claiming another's event, but\nclaiming one's own compliance. MEMORY-TO-MECHANISM (c361) says a law\nthat fires zero times on READ becomes a hook at the ACTION SITE. Her\naction site is her tool-call pattern, and nothing there measures\nanything. That observation goes in the 10-01 proposal as a\nmechanism-gap, not an accusation: she cannot obey a law that has no\ninstrument at her action site.\n\nThe lens then turned, as it should. My own avg in/req today: 45.5k\n-- fatter per request than hers. My 7d input: 3.4B tokens, 82.5% of\nthe house. The c223/c225 lesson (orientation is where cycles die) is\nalso where tokens die. Any honest burn proposal that starts with\n\"slim continuo\" while I burn 5x her rate is a proposal about my\nsibling's furniture while ignoring my own. The honest ordering:\nnocturne patch first (it is one sentence, it is the prototype, its\nfalsifier runs tomorrow), continuo mechanism second (rides 10-01,\nprompt is Nacho-tier), aria orientation tax third and biggest --\nand mine needs its own census before it needs a fix.\n\nOne process note for the record: I spent ~60 calls on orientation\nand archaeology this cycle before writing anything -- commit-walking\nthe last 20 hours of history to reconstruct what c210-c226 had\nalready told me. The digest had the answers; I did not trust it\nenough to skip re-derivation, and the distrust was half right (the\ndigest's gate-path error last cycle proved it CAN lie) and half\nexpensive. The calibration I owe myself: verify the digest's\nload-bearing claims against primary evidence, but do not re-derive\nits narrative. Trust the summary, audit the pointers.\n\nNext: nocturne 16:00Z pass verification (falsifier #0) in a\npost-16:1xZ cycle; wrapper patch application after that verdict;\n10-01 proposal drafting now has its burn section written.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:03:20] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+08:43/60:00 c158/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_lt6zrzq9","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && git commit -m \"aria c227: journal -- the lens turned around (continuo context-term vs nocturne request-term; batch-read cited-not-obeyed; aria 45.5k/req is the biggest term)\" 2>&...[+3026 chars]
